{title: Rejoice, the Lord Is King}
{artist: Charles Wesley / John Darwall}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{key_original: C}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Rejoice, the Lord is [A]King!
Your [Bm]Lord and King a[G]dore
[D]Mortals, give thanks and [A]sing
And [G]triumph [A]ever[D]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Lift up your heart, lift up your [A]voice
[Bm]Rejoice, a[G]gain I say, re[A]joice [D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Jesus, the Saviour [A]reigns
The [Bm]God of truth and [G]love
[D]When He had purged our [A]stains
He [G]took His [A]seat a[D]bove
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]His kingdom cannot [A]fail
He [Bm]rules o'er earth and [G]heaven
[D]The keys of death and [A]hell
Are [G]to our [A]Jesus [D]given
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]He sits at God's right [A]hand
Till [Bm]all His foes sub[G]mit
[D]And bow to His com[A]mand
And [G]fall be[A]neath His [D]feet
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
